       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Asthma:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " only w an ICS, never as monotx; ⍉for acute relief in an exacerbation. Dose 1–2 puffs every 12 h; synergistic w the ICS and permits a lower ICS dose."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Salmeterol (asthma, ≥ 4 y):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 1 inhalation BID w an ICS; EIB: 1 inhalation ≥ 30 min b4 exercise. ⍉extra LABA for any reason."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Tremor, anxiety, tachy, mild temp hypokalemia (same as SABAs). Using a long-acting agent prn or more than BID raises arrhythmia risk."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (ritonavir, ketoconazole): ⍉recommended (cardiovasc effects). MAOIs/TCAs: extreme caution. BBs: may block the effect and cause severe bronchospasm. Non–K-sparing diuretics: hypokalemia/ECG chgs may worsen."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "OD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " excess β stim (seizures, angina, tachy up to 200/min, arrhythmias, hypokalemia, hyperglycemia, met acidosis) and QTc prolongation w ventricular arrhythmias. Tx: stop the drug, Sxtomatic care, ♡ monitoring; a cardioselective BB may be considered judiciously."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
